messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 36 and 32? Please reason step by step.. I think the correct answer is: 1652\n', '<think>.\nTo find the product of 36 and 32, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. We can break down the numbers into their factors and then multiply them together.\n\n36 can be broken down into 30 and 6, and 32 can be broken down into 30 and 2. So, we can rewrite the multiplication as:.\n\n36 x 32 = (30 + 6) x (30 + 2).\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to expand the expression:.\n\n(30 + 6) x (30 + 2) = 30 x 30 + 30 x 2 + 6 x 30 + 6 x 2.\n\nNext, we can calculate each of the products:.\n\n30 x 30 = 900.\n30 x 2 = 60.\n6 x 30 = 180.\n6 x 2 = 12.\n\nFinally, we can add up all the products:.\n\n900 + 60 + 180 + 12 = 1152.\n\nSo, the product of 36 and 32 is 1152.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
